<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Nawaz Sharif</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">b. <a href="/years/1949">1949</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Mian Muhammad Nawaz Sharif</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Nawaz Sharif is a Pakistani industrialist and politician who served three times as prime minister, in 1990–93, 1997–99 and 2013–17. Leader of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/all-india-muslim-league">Muslim League</a> (N), he ordered Pakistan's nuclear tests in 1998. He was overthrown by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pervez-musharraf">Pervez Musharraf</a>'s coup in 1999 and disqualified from office by the Supreme Court in 2017.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/nawaz-sharif.jpg" alt="Nawaz Sharif" width="320" height="404" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Z A Balti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:PrimeMinisterNawazSharif.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
